# motoquencer: per-step CV randomization at the top detent (issue #57).
# motoquencer.md: "The other 7 steps will increasingly modify the step's CV by
# adding a different random offset each time the step is played. At position 7
# (the maximum), the offset is up to `cvrange`."
#
# SPEC-GAP (the manual names no distribution): the offset is BIPOLAR uniform,
# +/- (detent/7) * cvrange/2 around the stored pitch — so at detent 7 the offset
# spans a full cvrange peak-to-peak, "up to cvrange", half of it up and half down.
# It is drawn from the engine's seeded xorshift RNG (the same stream as the lucky
# operations and the gate probability), so `seed` pins it here.
#
# The arithmetic is arranged to show the raw draws: with continuous pitch
# (quantize 0, cvbase 0, cvrange 1) and the step dialed dead centre (0.5), the
# output is 0.5 + u * 0.5 where u is uniform in [-1, +1) — i.e. exactly the
# uniform [0, 1) draw itself. These are the seed-1 xorshift values, and they
# spread over the whole 0..1 cvrange around the dialed 0.5.
seed 1
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    numfaders = 1
    numsteps  = 1
    clock     = I1
    fadermode = I2
    quantize  = 0
    cvbase    = 0
    cvrange   = 1
    holdcv    = 0
    cv        = O1
>>>
# randomize lane (fadermode 1): top detent = 7 of 8
@1 set I2 1
@2 move F1 1.0
@3 expect F1 1.0 tol 1e-4
# back to the CV lane: dial the step to the centre of the range
@4 set I2 0
@5 move F1 0.5
@6 expect F1 0.5 tol 1e-4
# every step entry draws a fresh offset
@10 set I1 1
@10 expect O1 0.0000629 tol 1e-5
@11 set I1 0
@12 set I1 1
@12 expect O1 0.0157474 tol 1e-5
@13 set I1 0
@14 set I1 1
@14 expect O1 0.6164041 tol 1e-5
@15 set I1 0
@16 set I1 1
@16 expect O1 0.0716186 tol 1e-5
@17 set I1 0
@18 set I1 1
@18 expect O1 0.5584883 tol 1e-5
@19 set I1 0
@20 set I1 1
@20 expect O1 0.1735742 tol 1e-5
